Who's that?

00:38:21.840 --> 00:38:22.500
Ben Scramer.

00:38:23.300 --> 00:38:24.980
I made out with him once last fall.

00:38:25.380 --> 00:38:27.390
Because he heard about me and Ray.

00:38:28.060 --> 00:38:29.640
Well, here I go.

00:38:30.000 --> 00:38:40.820
back into the fire save my seat well she certainly bounces back fast it's with you gee i wonder what

00:38:41.490 --> 00:38:47.230
callie you're not actually mad because she's here are you well given that i didn't want you living

00:38:47.230 --> 00:38:51.280
with her do you really think i want her hanging around her boyfriend just broke up with her sarah

00:38:52.070 --> 00:38:58.130
have a little compassion it's amazing how you can make insensitivity sound so nice i'm insensitive

00:38:58.130 --> 00:38:58.710
me

00:39:02.330 --> 00:39:04.880
Man, Sarah, I finally find a place.

00:39:05.920 --> 00:39:09.130
One that I can afford with a roommate who actually seems pretty cool,

00:39:09.150 --> 00:39:10.890
and you don't even try and enjoy it for me.

00:39:10.950 --> 00:39:12.470
Given the details, can you blame me?

00:39:12.650 --> 00:39:16.820
Yes, I can, because I have never given you a reason not to trust me, ever.

00:39:18.550 --> 00:39:20.990
So I really don't think it's fair for you to guilt-trip me like this

00:39:20.990 --> 00:39:22.890
because I'm friends with my roommate.

00:39:23.090 --> 00:39:24.610
So I'm just supposed to be happy about it.

00:39:24.690 --> 00:39:25.390
Yes, you are.

00:39:26.160 --> 00:39:28.460
And if you can't be happy, then you should fake it.

00:39:47.560 --> 00:39:52.050
Hey, Coop, Julia.

00:39:53.190 --> 00:39:53.970
We were just gonna eat.

00:39:57.420 --> 00:39:59.970
You guys, you aren't-

00:40:00.000 --> 00:40:00.380
Want to join us?

00:40:03.130 --> 00:40:03.410
Yeah.

00:40:03.620 --> 00:40:04.020
Sure.

00:40:04.970 --> 00:40:05.270
Thanks.

00:40:19.010 --> 00:40:26.080
I was thinking, you know those award shows?

00:40:26.530 --> 00:40:29.640
Like the Academy Awards or the Grammys?

00:40:30.640 --> 00:40:35.080
You know how at those things they always give out, like, a special prize to somebody who overcame a tragedy?

00:40:36.170 --> 00:40:36.570
Yeah.

00:40:37.530 --> 00:40:43.570
And the tragedy person always says, most of all, I'd like to thank my wife, without whom I never would have made it.

00:40:46.910 --> 00:40:49.600
You think it's easy for those wives? Or husbands?

00:40:49.800 --> 00:40:53.550
I mean, you think being so supportive just comes naturally to them?

00:40:54.560 --> 00:40:59.980
Well, I doubt it's easy, but I bet if you love somebody...

00:41:00.000 --> 00:41:16.700
someone it comes pretty naturally kirsten's not doing any better joel really mornings are so so

00:41:16.700 --> 00:41:25.850
but afternoons and evenings are pretty unbearable i guess i talked to her doctor and he said she

00:41:25.850 --> 00:41:27.150
might be like this for a long time

00:41:37.290 --> 00:41:45.730
So I guess you just hang in there, however long it takes.

00:41:48.660 --> 00:41:49.240
I can't.

00:41:51.280 --> 00:41:52.680
What do you mean, of course you can?

00:41:54.140 --> 00:41:54.840
You don't know that.

00:41:56.300 --> 00:41:57.840
Think about it, when have I ever been good

00:41:57.840 --> 00:41:58.640
at hanging in there?

00:42:00.060 --> 00:42:03.000
Let's face it, if there's one thing I suck at, it's the long haul.

00:42:04.490 --> 00:42:06.570
That is so not true, Charlie.

00:42:06.980 --> 00:42:08.660
I mean, you hung in there for us.

00:42:09.340 --> 00:42:09.700
Barely.

00:42:10.550 --> 00:42:11.930
And only because I didn't have a choice.

00:42:22.140 --> 00:42:23.560
You know what I think this is like?

00:42:26.370 --> 00:42:29.960
This is like when we were little and we'd pack for our summer camping trip.

00:42:31.840 --> 00:42:35.660
I'd get out all my camping clothes from the year before and try them on.

00:42:37.670 --> 00:42:42.840
And each year I'd be really surprised that they were too small

00:42:42.840 --> 00:42:45.190
because I hadn't even noticed that I'd grown.

00:42:51.100 --> 00:42:51.820
You've noticed.

00:42:52.300 --> 00:42:58.360
You're so scared I'm going to want to bail on her.

00:43:04.830 --> 00:43:05.550
You know what, Charlie?

00:43:07.320 --> 00:43:07.580
Not.
